<main>
<section id="home">
  <div class="profile-heading">
    <a href="images/whiteshirt_aaysharma.jpg"><img src="images/circle_cropped_whiteshirt_aaysharma.png" alt="Amatya Sharma" class="home-photo" width="152" height="152"></a>
    <div>
      <h1 class="name-heading">Amatya Sharma</h1>
      <p class="profile-affiliation">Ph.D. Candidate, Theoretical Computer Science<br><a href="https://umich.edu/">University of Michigan, Ann Arbor</a><br><a href="mailto:amatya@umich.edu">amatya@umich.edu</a></p>
      <p class="profile-meta">Expected graduation: April 2027</p>
      <div class="social-links" aria-label="Academic profiles">
        <a class="cv-link" href="data/Amatya_Sharma_CV_latest_pdf.pdf">Download CV</a>
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=FN6Q_jEAAAAJ&amp;hl=en">Scholar</a>
        <a href="https://dblp.org/pid/279/6355.html">DBLP</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/amatya-sharma/">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
      <p class="statement-link"><a href="research-statement.html">Research Statement</a> <span class="statement-status">(Work in progress)</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="home-intro">
    <p>I am a Ph.D. candidate in <a href="https://theory.engin.umich.edu/">Theoretical Computer Science</a> at the University of Michigan, fortunate to be co-advised by <a href="https://bansal.engin.umich.edu/">Nikhil Bansal</a> and <a href="https://web.eecs.umich.edu/~euiwoong/">Euiwoong Lee</a>. I received my B.Tech. and M.Tech. in Computer Science from <a href="http://www.iitkgp.ac.in/">IIT Kharagpur</a>.</p>
    <p>My research interests include approximation, streaming, online, and parameterized algorithms, with a focus on constraint satisfaction problems, clustering, and combinatorial optimization.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="news">
<h2 class="section-title">Recent news</h2>
<div class="recent-news">
<div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">2027</div><div class="news-text">Incoming long-term visitor at the <strong>Simons Institute, UC Berkeley</strong>, January–April, for <em>Symmetry in Efficient Computation with Local Constraints</em>.</div></div>
<div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">2027</div><div class="news-text">Incoming participant in the <strong>Iliad Intensive</strong> in Berkeley, January 4–29.</div></div>
<div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">2027</div><div class="news-text"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.14654">Spectral Dual Fitting for <i>k</i>-Means</a> will appear at <strong>SODA 2027</strong>.</div></div>
<div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">2026</div><div class="news-text">Our ESA paper on streaming CSPs was invited to a special issue of <em>Theoretical Computer Science</em>.</div></div>
</div>
<details class="expandable quiet-expander"><summary>Earlier news</summary><div class="expanded-content"><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Aug 2026]</div><div class="news-text">Presented my work on Streaming CSPs in ESA 2026.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[2025]</div><div class="news-text">Visited TTIC in September–October 2025, working with Santhoshini Velusamy.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Aug 2025]</div><div class="news-text">Presented our paper on MinCSPs on Complete Instances II at APPROX 2025.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Jan 2025]</div><div class="news-text">Presented our paper on MinCSPs on Complete Instances at SODA 2025.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Dec 2024]</div><div class="news-text">A Decomposition Approach to the Weighted k-server Problem appeared at FSTTCS 2024.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Aug 2024]</div><div class="news-text">Served as a Teaching Assistant for EECS 477: Introduction to Algorithms.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Aug 2023]</div><div class="news-text">Organized Theory Talks and Lunches at University of Michigan.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Aug 2022]</div><div class="news-text">Joined the Computer Science Ph.D. program at <a href="https://umich.edu/">University of Michigan, Ann Arbor</a>.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Mar 2022]</div><div class="news-text">Received Ph.D. offers from University of Michigan, Georgia Tech, University of Toronto, and EPFL.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Jul 2021]</div><div class="news-text">Received a full-time pre-placement offer from Oracle R&D, Bangalore.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[May 2021]</div><div class="news-text">Presented Guillotine Separable Packings for 2D Knapsack at HALG 2021.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Apr 2021]</div><div class="news-text">Interned at Oracle R&D from May to July 2021.</div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Feb 2021]</div><div class="news-text">SoCG 2021 paper accepted — first SoCG paper from IIT Kharagpur in 26 years. <a href="https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.48">paper</a></div></div><div class="news-item"><div class="news-date">[Nov 2020]</div><div class="news-text">First publication: Liquid Democracy at CALDAM 2021. <a href="https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-67899-9_7">paper</a></div></div></div></details>
</section>

<section id="pubs">
<h2 class="section-title">Publications &amp; manuscripts</h2>
<p class="section-note">Authors are listed alphabetically by surname, following the theory-CS convention.</p>
<h3 class="subsection-title">Published &amp; accepted papers</h3>
<ol class="paper-list">
<li>
<article class="publication paper">
  <div class="publication-content">
    <h3>Spectral Dual Fitting for k-Means</h3>
    <p class="paper-authors">Aditya Anand, Moses Charikar, Vincent Cohen-Addad, Ruiquan Gao, Fabrizio Grandoni, Euiwoong Lee, Amatya Sharma, Ernest van Wijland</p>
    <p class="publication-venue">SODA 2027.</p>
    <div class="publication-icons"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.14654" title="arXiv preprint">arXiv</a></div>
    <details class="paper-abstract"><summary>Abstract</summary><p>
          A new dual fitting algorithm which gives improved approximation ratios of 3+ln2+ϵ (≈3.694) and 4.9+ϵ for k-Means in (high-dimensional) Euclidean and general metrics respectively.        </p></details>
  </div>
</article>
</li>
<li>
<article class="publication paper">
  <div class="publication-content">
    <h3>Characterizing Streaming Decidability of CSPs via Non-Redundancy</h3>
    <p class="paper-authors">Amatya Sharma, Santhoshini Velusamy</p>
    <p class="publication-venue">ESA 2026. Invited to a special issue of Theoretical Computer Science.</p>
    <div class="publication-icons"><a href="https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2026.131" title="Conference Proceeding">Paper</a> <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21922" title="arXiv preprint">arXiv</a> <a href="data/streaming_csp_decidability.pdf" title="ESA Presentation">Slides</a></div>
    <details class="paper-abstract"><summary>Abstract</summary><p>
            Characterizes the single-pass streaming complexity of CSP satisfiability, up to logarithmic factors, by the non-redundancy of the constraint language.
          </p></details>
  </div>
</article>
</li>
<li>
<article class="publication paper">
  <div class="publication-content">
    <h3>Min CSPs on Complete Instances II: A Polylogarithmic Approximation for NAE-3-SAT</h3>
    <p class="paper-authors">Aditya Anand, Euiwoong Lee, Davide Mazzali, Amatya Sharma</p>
    <p class="publication-venue">APPROX 2025.</p>
    <div class="publication-icons"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.19051" title="arXiv preprint">arXiv</a> <a href="data/APPROX_NAE.pdf" title="Presentation at APPROX">Slides</a></div>
    <details class="paper-abstract"><summary>Abstract</summary><p>
            We continue the study of complete instances for minimization constraint satisfaction problems and give a polylogarithmic approximation for Min-Not-All-Equal-3-SAT on complete instances.
          </p></details>
  </div>
</article>
</li>
<li>
<article class="publication paper">
  <div class="publication-content">
    <h3>Min CSPs on Complete Instances</h3>
    <p class="paper-authors">Aditya Anand, Euiwoong Lee, Amatya Sharma</p>
    <p class="publication-venue">SODA 2025.</p>
    <div class="publication-icons"><a href="https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611978322.35" title="Official SODA version">Paper</a> <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.19066" title="arXiv preprint">arXiv</a> <a href="data/MinCSPs.pdf" title="Presentation at SODA">Slides</a></div>
    <details class="paper-abstract"><summary>Abstract</summary><p>
            We initiate the study of complete instances for minimization constraint satisfaction problems and prove algorithmic results for Min-2CSP and related k-CSPs.
          </p></details>
  </div>
</article>
</li>
<li>
<article class="publication paper">
  <div class="publication-content">
    <h3>A Decomposition Approach to the Weighted k-server Problem</h3>
    <p class="paper-authors">Nikhil Ayyadevara, Ashish Chiplunkar, Amatya Sharma</p>
    <p class="publication-venue">FSTTCS 2024.</p>
    <div class="publication-icons"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.06485">arXiv</a> <a href="https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSTTCS.2024.6">Paper</a></div>
    <details class="paper-abstract"><summary>Abstract</summary><p>
            We present a decomposition approach for the online weighted k-server problem.
          </p></details>
  </div>
</article>
</li>
<li>
<article class="publication paper">
  <div class="publication-content">
    <h3>Two-Dimensional Guillotine Strip Packing</h3>
    <p class="paper-authors">Arindam Khan, Aditya Lonkar, Arnab Maiti, Amatya Sharma, Andreas Wiese</p>
    <p class="publication-venue">ICALP 2022.</p>
    <div class="publication-icons"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.05989">arXiv</a></div>
    <details class="paper-abstract"><summary>Abstract</summary><p>
            We give a (3/2 + ε)-approximation algorithm for 2D Strip Packing in a guillotine-separable setting, including a PPTAS.
          </p></details>
  </div>
</article>
</li>
<li>
<article class="publication paper">
  <div class="publication-content">
    <h3>On Guillotine Separable Packings for the 2D Geometric Knapsack Problem</h3>
    <p class="paper-authors">Arindam Khan, Arnab Maiti, Amatya Sharma, Andreas Wiese</p>
    <p class="publication-venue">SoCG 2021; contributed talk at HALG 2021.</p>
    <div class="publication-icons"><a href="https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.48" title="Official SoCG version">Paper</a> <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.09735" title="arXiv preprint">arXiv</a> <a href="data/SOCG-Final-PPT.pdf" title="Presentation at SoCG 2021">Slides (SoCG)</a> <a href="data/MONDAY_SHARMA.pdf" title="Presentation at HALG 2021">Slides (HALG)</a> <a href="data/MONDAY_SHARMA_POSTER.pdf" title="Research poster">Poster</a></div>
    <details class="paper-abstract"><summary>Abstract</summary><p>
            We give a PPTAS for the 2D Knapsack problem in a guillotine-separable setting, improving over the previous best approximation factor of 3.
          </p></details>
  </div>
</article>
</li>
<li>
<article class="publication paper">
  <div class="publication-content">
    <h3>On Parameterized Complexity of Liquid Democracy</h3>
    <p class="paper-authors">Palash Dey, Arnab Maiti, Amatya Sharma</p>
    <p class="publication-venue">CALDAM 2021.</p>
    <div class="publication-icons"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.14192">arXiv</a> <a href="https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-67899-9_7">Paper</a> <a href="https://youtu.be/JFnH7nRP6XQ">Video</a></div>
    <details class="paper-abstract"><summary>Abstract</summary><p>
            We study parameterized algorithms for Liquid Democracy, a voting system where voters may delegate their votes.
          </p></details>
  </div>
</article>
</li>
